<h2 id="ha-ctrl-003-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Test a 0.5-unit step, a negative range and exact endpoints. Verify the accessible value and native formatted display agree.
2. Use only a keyboard to adjust and reach any essential action configured for hold or double tap. Test touch without relying on hover.
3. Load unknown and unavailable values; neither may announce a numeric minimum as a reading.
4. Change capabilities and reported values during an edit. Check duplicate request prevention, error recovery, zoom and theme removal without overwriting native control behaviour.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

